     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The model in section 8.13 (pg 145 &amp; 146) demonstrates how to take in a matrix of predictors as I believe you want. You need to declare X to be a Nx2 matrix in the data block, beta as a Nx2 matrix in the parameters block, nix the creation of mu, and simply do:<div><br></div><div>    y ~ normal( rows_dot_product( x , beta[subj] ) , sigma) ;<br></div><div><br></div><div>in the parameters block.</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><br>--<br>Mike Lawrence<br>Graduate Student<br>Department of Psychology &amp; Neuroscience<br>Dalhousie University<br><br>~ Certainty is (possibly) folly ~</div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div>"
