    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Feb 23, 2017 at 10:14 PM, Mike Lawrence <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mike....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">The model in section 8.13 (pg 145 &amp; 146) demonstrates how to take in a matrix of predictors as I believe you want. You need to declare X to be a Nx2 matrix in the data block, beta as a Nx2 matrix in the parameters block, nix the creation of mu, and simply do:<div><br></div><div>    y ~ normal( rows_dot_product( x , beta[subj] ) , sigma) ;<br></div><div><br></div><div>in the parameters block.</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><br>--<br>Mike Lawrence<br>Graduate Student<br>Department of Psychology &amp; Neuroscience<br>Dalhousie University<br><br>~ Certainty is (possibly) folly ~</div></div><div><div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Feb 23, 2017 at 6:59 PM, Luca Campanelli <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">campan...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Stan users, <br>I’d like my model to work with different number of predictors - it’s a multilevel model with repeated observations nested within subject. Don’t know if I’m missing something simple, but I tried different solutions and they don’t seem to work. <br><br>This is what I have: <br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// number of observations</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n_subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// number of subjects</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// subject indicator</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">          </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// predictor</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n_subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n_subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    <br>    y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><br><br>Below is my new version (that doesn’t work) where I’m trying to get one beta by subject (as above) and for each predictor in the matrix X. <br>I receive the following error message: “base type mismatch in assignment; variable name = mu, type = real; right-hand side type=matrix”<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// number of observations</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n_subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// number of subjects</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// subject indicator</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    row_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> X</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// predictors matrix</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">// Note that X is a matrix: </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">//   Intercept    x</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">//           1    0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">//           1    0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">//           1    1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">//           1    1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">//           …    … </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n_subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">subj</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> X</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    <br>    y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><br><br>Declaring beta as<br>    row_vector[2] beta[J];<br>still doesn’t work. <br><br>Thank you in advance for any suggestion you may have to fix this issue or find some other way to achieve the same goal. <br><span><font color=